	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "ESP32-C3 SuperMini development module, mounted as an SMD part on two rows of eight 3.025 x 1.524 mm pads at 2.54 mm pitch, 15.97 mm between rows. Board 18 x 22.7 mm with the USB-C end notched. Pad names are the module's own silkscreen labels (5V, G, 3.3, 0-10, 20, 21) rather than numbers, so design.py refers to pins like U3.3.3 and U3.G. Brought in from a machine-local library at C:/dev/kicad/libs, originally a SnapEDA/SamacSys download, so that the project resolves without it. The 3D model was not attached in the original and is wired up here: the STEP is Y-up like the rest of that vendor's models, hence rotate -90 about X, and its seating plane is the module PCB bottom at Y=0 so no offset is needed - the geometry below that plane is the through-hole pin stubs.")
	(tags "esp32-c3 supermini module esp32 riscv wifi ble smd")
